messages:
customer_jordan: Hey team — streaming responses from the Node/Edge SDK keep stalling for our Next.js Edge function behind Cloudflare Access. First chunk arrives, then nothing. Happens only in prod, not locally.

emma_support: Sorry you're hitting that, Jordan. Can you share the SDK version and a minimal repro? Also whether you rotate tokens server-side (short-lived creds)? :thinking_face:

customer_jordan: Using redwood-edge-sdk@0.9.1 (installed via package.json). We do token rotation every 10m with a proxy that injects Authorization. Repro steps: deploy to Vercel Edge, enable Cloudflare Access in front, hit endpoint. Works for ~2-3 chunks, then stream stops yielding. No 502s, connection stays open.

emma_support: Got it. Do you see any 401s in the proxy logs / any token swap logs when it stalls? Also curious if you're using streaming via ReadableStream.getReader() or async iterator.

customer_jordan: We use ReadableStream async iterator: for await (const chunk of res.body) { /* append */ }. Proxy logs show no 401. Only thing in Vercel logs: "client closed connection" sometimes after 30s.

supportbot: New support ticket created: #SUP-8271 (escalated to Eng).

ryan_eng: Hi Jordan — quick q: does the repro use HTTP/2 or upgrade via h2->h1 proxy? Cloudflare Access can terminate/translate protocols. Also can you paste the minimal fetch code you're using in the Edge function?

customer_jordan: Sure, here's the handler (simplified):

```js
export default async function handler(req) {
  const r = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/stream', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_TOKEN}` },
    body: JSON.stringify({ model: 'gpt-small', prompt: 'hi' })
  });
  const reader = r.body.getReader();
  while (true) {
    const { value, done } = await reader.read();
    if (done) break;
    // send chunk to client via response stream
  }
}
```

ryan_eng: Thanks — that helps. Two hypotheses: (1) older SDK version (0.9.x) had a retry wrapper that reissued requests on transient 5xxs but didn't reattach the original streaming consumer properly, causing a silent stall when the underlying stream switched sockets. (2) Cloudflare Access is buffering/chunk coalescing and when token rotation happens the proxy injects a new header mid-stream causing the SDK retry to refresh the request (silent behind the fetch) and the original ReadableStream reader is left attached to dead underlying body.

emma_support: Can you confirm if you rotate tokens on the same connection? If the proxy rewrites Authorization and triggers any 401->refresh flow, that matches the retry hypothesis.

customer_jordan: We rotate by swapping a header on the edge proxy every 10m, not on the connection itself. But we do see rotation events in auth logs around the same time as stalls.

ryan_eng: Okay. Two immediate tests: (A) upgrade to redwood-edge-sdk@0.10.2 (we fixed a streaming retry bug in that patch) and (B) try using the async iterator pattern instead of getReader to see if behavior differs:

```js
for await (const chunk of r.body) {
  // same append
}
```

emma_support: Also, can you enable DEBUG=http*,redwood* in your Edge function env and redeploy so we can capture SDK logs when the stall occurs?

customer_jordan: Will try upgrade + debug and report back in ~30m. Appreciate the quick triage. :pray:

supportbot: Escalation update: assign to eng-ryan, priority P2, linked ticket SUP-8271.

emma_support: If upgrade fixes it, we'll roll a support note. If not, Ryan will request a minimal repro we can run behind Cloudflare Access to reproduce the exact proxy rewrite pattern.

customer_jordan: OK upgraded to 0.10.2 and switched to for-await. Re-deployed — looks stable so far after 12 minutes (previously would die by ~2-3m). Will keep testing.

ryan_eng: Great news. If this stays green, we'll mark as fix in 0.10.2: "fix(streaming): avoid silent retry path that dropped ReadableStream reader on retry", and follow up on docs for token rotation patterns behind proxies.

customer_jordan: Thanks everyone, saved my Friday. :tada:
